    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0415" n="327" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg327"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-02-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                    1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Choate states that Lord Lansdowne asks whether Manchuria is within the
                    phrase “neutrality of China” and whether it is under <pb facs="0416" n="328"
                        xml:id="pg328"/> stood that Japan should preclude herself from activity in
                    that province of China in spite of Russia’s occupation and of which the latter
                    might make use as a base of military operations.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
